        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "82743217-919f-5cc8-8023-688c2417b43d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cranford (TV series), Cranford (novel)\n- People: Simon Curtis, Steve Hudson, Heidi Thomas, Elizabeth Gaskell, Charles Dickens\n- Works: My Lady Ludlow, Mr Harrison's Confessions, Household Words\n- Topics: television adaptation, publication history\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Gaskell published the novellas \"Cranford,\" \"My Lady Ludlow,\" and \"Mr Harrison's Confessions\" between 1849 and 1858.\n- Elizabeth Gaskell's novel \"Cranford\" was first published irregularly in eight instalments between December 1851 and May 1853 in the magazine \"Household Words.\"\n- Charles Dickens edited the magazine \"Household Words\" when Elizabeth Gaskell's \"Cranford\" appeared there.\n- \"Cranford\" is one of the better-known novels by 19th-century English writer Elizabeth Gaskell.\n- The British television series \"Cranford\" was directed by Simon Curtis and Steve Hudson.\n- Heidi Thomas adapted the teleplay for the television series \"Cranford\" from Elizabeth Gaskell's three novellas \"Cranford,\" \"My Lady Ludlow,\" and \"Mr Harrison's Confessions.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
